to the surface.

(''c'') If we choose the initial conditions in equation (5) so that the coefficients <math>\text{C}_1</math> and <math>\text{C}_2</math> are zero, then the equation will become—
{{block center|<math>\theta = \Theta \,.\, \frac{1}{1 - \frac{\text{T}^2}{\text{T}_1^2}} \sin \frac{\pi}{\text{T}_1} t.</math>}}
Since <math>\theta_1</math>, the slope of the wave, is equal to <math>\Theta_1 \sin \frac{\pi}{\text{T}_1} t</math>, the ratio of the ship's angle to the vertical to the angle that the normal to the wave-slope makes with the vertical, or <math>\theta/\theta_1</math>,
{{block center|<math>= \frac{1}{1 - \frac{\text{T}^2}{\text{T}_1^2}} = \text{constant}.</math>}}
